    "I'll read the document first.\n<message to=\"discord-main\">\n**Q3 Platform Review — five-point summary**\n\n1. **Availability missed target.** 99.82% uptime vs. a 99.9% goal, driven by two incidents: a 41-minute database failover (12 Aug) and a 22-minute CDN misconfiguration (3 Sep).\n\n2. **Infrastructure spend ran 6% over budget.** $418K against $394K, with the overage concentrated in egress charges.\n\n3. **Adoption grew but thinned out.** Weekly active teams rose 40% (1,240 → 1,733), while seat utilisation inside those teams fell from 71% to 64%.\n\n4. **Support held its SLA under higher load.** Ticket volume up 18% to 2,904, yet median first response was 3.1 hours against a 4-hour commitment.\n\n5. **Two risks carry into Q4.** The egress overage is expected to persist without a caching change, and the utilisation drop alongside team growth points to shallow adoption.\n</message>",
